# There is no merge rule for the log, and the absence is the decision
# (ADR-25f977377fa0). `.ank/log/** merge=union` used to be here, and it was
# right for what it named: a file appended to by two branches is the textbook
# adjacent-change conflict, three texts in this repository claimed git resolved
# it on its own, and nothing configured one. An entry is an entity now, so two
# concurrent entries are two new files and there is nothing for a three-way
# merge to be three-way about. The rule was removed rather than left because a
# merge rule for a path no writer produces is a claim about a shape that is
# gone; the property that protects the corpus is one file per entity, which
# comes from the addressing and holds whatever git does.

# The one exception, and it has to be one: this fixture's content *is* its line
# endings. Under the rule above git would hand it back in LF on every checkout
# and the CRLF test would pass while testing nothing. `-text` means no
# conversion in either direction -- the bytes committed are the bytes read.
crates/ank-core/tests/golden/valid/TASK-c71f0e5a9b23.md -text
